n","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-03-10T14:27:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-25T16:52:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6.1 and master commit 29b945f2eb.\n\n### System information\n\nCachyOS AMD Radeon 890M Mesa 26.0.1\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen moving an object over transparent bakground in an XR scene, the object pixels are not cleared when the object moves, resulting in permanent \"background coloring\".\nThis bug arises with Mesa version 26.0.1 as version 25.X.X runs fine.\nUsing RADV_DEBUG=nodcc solves the issue.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nJust start the scene with an XR headset.\nI'm using WiVRN to connect my headset, but it works fine with other programs like hello_xr or xr_gears.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[xr-transparency-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25872851/xr-transparency-bug.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117292/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117292/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}